WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:05.640
You can attempt to flee, you can try your
best to hide, you might even valiantly try

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:10.480
to fight back, but when the bloody dawn of
the Scarlet King finally stretches across

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:16.410
the multiverse’s collective horizon, there
will be almost nothing that we can do.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:21.820
Every sadistic monster, every world-ending
horror, every dimension-transcending malicious

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:27.330
reality warper, none of them even begin to
approach the danger and pure, undiluted evil

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.500
of the Crimson Khan himself.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:35.370
We’ve covered this horrific eldritch entity
in several videos before - from his SCP-001

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:40.470
proposal, to the potential SCP identities
of his hellish spawn, to the earthly vectors

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:44.920
for those children: The horrifying SCP-231.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:49.540
But today, we’re not interested in once
again going over how the SCP Foundation feels

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.030
about their greatest enemy.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.070
That’s only one side of the story.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:58.140
Today, we’re going to explore the origins
of the Scarlet King through the cold, dark

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:03.540
eyes of a very different source: His very
first earthly worshippers.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.799
It all began with the Daevites.

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:10.679
We’ve discussed this extinct culture before
on this channel in passing, but to fully understand

00:01:10.679 --> 00:01:15.340
how we know the cursed information we’re
imparting today, we first need to understand

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.969
exactly who the Daevites are, and why they
were such a terrifying society.

00:01:19.969 --> 00:01:23.850
We’re not talking about a mere Group of
Interest here like the Serpent’s Hand or

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:29.289
the Chaos Insurgency, we’re talking about
an imperialistic, militarist civilization

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:34.840
that brought pain, terror, and suffering to
everyone and everything they encountered.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.640
The Daevite culture was arranged into a series
of dense, urban city-states that supported

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:44.250
themselves through brutal slave labor, farmed
from their own people and weaker groups that

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.380
they conquered through extremely hostile takeovers.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:52.460
The name “Daevites” is derived from the
culture’s ruling class, the Daevas, powerful

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:57.759
and potentially immortal sorcerers who maintained
their abilities through ritualistic torture,

00:01:57.759 --> 00:02:00.249
sacrifice, and cannibalism.

00:02:00.249 --> 00:02:04.469
Much of what we know about these monsters
is derived from a cursed book titled “A

00:02:04.469 --> 00:02:10.649
Chronicle of the Daevas”, designated by
the SCP Foundation as SCP-140, an incomplete

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:11.680
chronicle.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.650
Much like its subjects, the book is bloodthirsty.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:19.130
Ink or human blood spilled around the book
will be stolen and incorporated into text

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.200
on its sordid pages.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:26.780
That would be ominous enough, but it gets
much worse: As editions of the book are “revised”

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:32.700
through these sanguine updates, the book literally
revises the history of the real world, moving

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.730
the extinction date of the Daevites just that
much closer.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:40.470
The book is one of the Foundation’s most
closely guarded anomalies because if enough

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:45.560
revisions are made that the Daevite culture
enters recent history, or even worse, the

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:49.680
present day, it would mean the end of the
world as we know it.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.890
In all likelihood, the lucky ones among us
would be killed or written out of history

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:54.890
immediately.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:03:00.310
The rest would become slaves to the Daevas,
or become victims to their occult bloodlust.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:04.430
After finding out all this about these horrifying
people, it really shouldn’t come as a surprise

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:08.880
to you that they’re some of the first recorded
worshippers of the Scarlet King in our dimension.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:13.060
You’d have trouble finding a more perfect
representation of the King’s philosophy

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:18.660
around pain, cruelty, subjugation, and a world
ruled by primitive violence.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:22.850
That brings us to what we can learn about
the King himself from artifacts left behind

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.490
by his first and most ardent followers.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:30.220
A collection of tablets that act as a kind
of sacred, holy creation myth for the Scarlet

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:36.000
King and his gruesome pantheon was discovered
at a Foundation-sponsored Daevite dig site,

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:41.710
and using other Daevite sources, these tablets
were translated into a harrowing account known

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:45.020
only as Dust and Blood...

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:49.770
Between the darkness below and the darkness
above, at the beginning of all things, the

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.900
Tree of Life was planted.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:56.290
This was the moment when all things across
the multiverse were given form.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.710
Life and death began.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.630
Expansion and entropy.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.470
Order and chaos.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:08.750
And out of all that, a caste of Elder Gods
was also born in the vast and quivering dark.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:12.770
Many of their names have been lost to the
pages of history, but one that was not was

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.870
a being known only as Khahrahk.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.949
Khahrahk was born into humble beginnings.

00:04:17.949 --> 00:04:22.699
He and his forgotten siblings roiled in the
abyss, the only thing separating him from

00:04:22.699 --> 00:04:27.490
everything else being the very awareness that
he was stuck down in the abyss.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:32.819
He was both blessed and cursed with self-awareness
in a void filled with ignorant darkness.

00:04:32.819 --> 00:04:36.610
He felt the sting of loneliness, pain, and
resentment.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:40.650
And if existence was such pain, what was the
point of existing at all?

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:45.740
In fact, what was the point of anyone or anything
existing, if they were all just doomed to

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.509
this dull suffering?

00:04:47.509 --> 00:04:53.460
At this moment, Khahrahk found his calling:
Bringing about the end of everything.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.800
But first, he needed strength.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:00.629
To achieve this, he devoured his brothers
and sisters in the abyss, stealing their strength

00:05:00.629 --> 00:05:02.400
and their essence.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:06.610
This is known as the First Sin of Khahrahk,
and he was punished accordingly with even

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.770
greater pain as he grew.

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:12.099
And of course, this did nothing but strengthen
his resolve.

00:05:12.099 --> 00:05:17.889
Blinded by pain, fury, and pure hatred, he
vowed to uproot and destroy the very tree

00:05:17.889 --> 00:05:21.419
of life itself for putting him through this
awfulness.

00:05:21.419 --> 00:05:23.669
This was Khahrahk’s first bloody conquest.

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:28.580
He clawed his way up to his throne, slaying
and devouring countless other Elder Gods over

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:31.099
eons of brutality and war.

00:05:31.099 --> 00:05:35.410
Some were allowed to live for showing loyalty
to Khahrahk, and they would amass great power

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:39.560
under him, but it would only ever be under
him.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:43.879
He was beginning to form what would later
become his legion of terrifying, supernatural

00:05:43.879 --> 00:05:45.530
warriors and servants.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:50.539
When his conquest of the Lower Realms of Creation
was complete, he gave himself the title of

00:05:50.539 --> 00:05:52.720
King of the Darkness Below.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:56.449
He also took the name Khnith-hgor, to reflect
his new position.

00:05:56.449 --> 00:06:00.839
His Kingdom of absolute cruelty and despair
would claim the souls of anyone unlucky enough

00:06:00.839 --> 00:06:06.289
to stray too close, and put them through the
suffering that Khnith-hgor had so resented.

00:06:06.289 --> 00:06:07.930
But his work wasn’t done.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:10.279
He was just getting started.

00:06:10.279 --> 00:06:15.650
The King of the Darkness Below declared all-out
war on the rest of creation, opening the floodgates

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:19.439
and releasing his terrifying forces on the
surrounding kingdoms.

00:06:19.439 --> 00:06:23.979
Their operations were the template for the
Daevite way of warfare and life: They would

00:06:23.979 --> 00:06:28.600
conquer and destroy, and force the survivors
into servitude.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:32.809
Anyone who dared defy the orders of the King
would be broken and destroyed.

00:06:32.809 --> 00:06:37.050
His word was law, and the law was absolute.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:41.279
At some point during the expansion of his
empire, Khnith-hgor enslaved a wise and beautiful

00:06:41.279 --> 00:06:45.060
goddess known as Sanna, or the Mother of Those
Beneath Us.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:50.080
She detested the King and his seemingly limitless
barbarism, but she was smart enough to follow

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:54.870
his orders and feign loyalty to ensure her
continued survival in the short term.

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:57.919
This, however, would not ensure her safety
forever.

00:06:57.919 --> 00:07:02.610
Khnith-hgor had no intention of ruling and
conquering alone; he wished to create an evil

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:08.110
dynasty to rule underneath him, and carry
out his every command across the multiverse.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:13.360
He decided that Sanna would be his first bride,
and forebearer to the first generation of

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:14.599
his spawn.

00:07:14.599 --> 00:07:19.369
She was made to lay with him for seven days
and seven nights, so that she could give birth

00:07:19.369 --> 00:07:25.310
to seven children - seven being a highly significant
number in the world of sorcery, and particularly

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:27.300
in the world of Khnith-hgor.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:31.960
Once Sanna had served this purpose, Khnith-hgor,
who could not feel anything even close to

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:36.289
love, had no more use for her, and crushed
her to death.

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:40.879
When he rose up from the grisly deed, his
armor was covered in Sanna’s blood.

00:07:40.879 --> 00:07:47.610
This striking image inspired his final name:
Shormaush Urdal, the Scarlet King.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:52.720
From Sanna, the Scarlet King gained seven
daughters, who in an act of further monstrosity,

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:55.300
he also made his seven brides.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:08:00.240
Each gave birth to a legion of nightmares,
which would become the Scarlet King’s most

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.159
loyal and dangerous soldiers.

00:08:02.159 --> 00:08:08.319
The Scarlet King also gave each of these brides
a sacred seal, so that they would never die.

00:08:08.319 --> 00:08:12.400
The first bride was A’tivik, who was the
favorite of the Scarlet King despite having

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:14.039
the smallest brood.

00:08:14.039 --> 00:08:18.909
She and her children were granted great wisdom
that would guide them to victory in battle.

00:08:18.909 --> 00:08:21.379
Her seal was vaduk, “dominion.”

00:08:21.379 --> 00:08:25.889
The second bride was A’ghor, born with a
great hole in her soul that left her forever

00:08:25.889 --> 00:08:26.939
in want.

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:32.070
However, she gave birth to a huge legion,
who then begot even greater armies to go forth

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.060
and conquer in the name of their terrible
grandfather.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:37.640
Her seal was kifenn, “longing.”

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:42.600
The third bride was A’distat, a creature
of unparalleled malice and hatred that extended

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:44.890
to even her own sisters.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:50.080
She and her brood were unmatched in their
ability to spread desolation, destruction,

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:52.180
and pestilence on the battlefield.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:53.890
Her seal was hezhum, “desolation.”

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:59.660
The fourth bride was A’zieb, a great berserker
if ever there was one.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:03.800
She took the form of a huge beast, as did
all her children.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:08.800
They would rampage through enemy forces, killing
scores of soldiers yet seeming impervious

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.880
to all damage dealt against them.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.770
Her seal was ba, “wrath.”

00:09:13.770 --> 00:09:18.820
The fifth bride was A’nuht, a beast with
a frail body but an incredible mind.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:23.530
Her children all proved to be adept sorcerers,
with the ability to craft and rework reality

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:25.360
however they pleased.

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:29.500
This would prove to be a great asset to the
Scarlet King, but he also feared that their

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:34.840
powers would allow them to rebel against him,
and so, he had them all crippled.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.740
Her seal was ner, “lack.”

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:43.140
The sixth bride was A’tellif, the most silent
and secretive of all the Scarlet Siblings.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:48.090
Her children had the remarkable ability to
change their faces, and walk unnoticed among

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:49.260
their enemies.

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:53.530
They also had the ability to open the Ways
between worlds, allowing the Scarlet King’s

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:56.410
endless war to spread across dimensions.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:59.280
Her seal was usheq, “hidden.”

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:04.820
And the seventh and final bride was A’habbat,
who was physically the weakest of them all,

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:09.540
but the only one with the strength of spirit
to disagree with and rebel against her father’s

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:10.840
diabolical wishes.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:15.720
Her children were brave warriors and hunters,
many of which are aligned with her mission

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.240
to stop the dreaded Scarlet King.

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:21.550
Though thus far, none have yet achieved this
lofty mission.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:24.160
Her seal was xokib, “hope.”

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:28.980
As the Scarlet King’s power grew, more of
the multiverse fell into his poisonous clutches,

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:31.870
rotting the very roots of the Tree of Life.

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:36.350
As the seven brides and their legions spread
out, they recruited more cosmic power players

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:38.660
for their grand war effort.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:43.150
The Hanged King pledged his allegiance, the
Prince of Many Faces swore his loyalty to

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:48.570
the Scarlet King, the demonic forces of The
Factory worked in the name of the unholy monarch,

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:52.300
and the horned demon lord Moloch bowed his
mighty head.

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:56.440
The Daevites firmly believed that the victory
of their almighty Scarlet King was as certain

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:58.080
as the sunset.

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:03.320
No matter what opposes him - be it the Serpent,
the Broken God, the arrogant fools like the

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:07.850
SCP Foundation - he and his forces will fight
on.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:15.080
They will tear the Tree of Life asunder, carving
away at everything until nothing remains.

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:20.030
Existence will be at its end, and the last
sound the multiverse ever hears will be the

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:24.840
Scarlet King himself sighing in relief after
a job well done.

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.340
He’ll finally be at peace.

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:30.520
Unless, of course, somebody stops him.

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:35.110
If the best minds the Foundation has to offer,
with all of its resources and knowledge and

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:39.030
connections, are able to create some kind
of weapon or shield against him.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:44.530
If SCP-999 truly is the child of A’habbat,
prophesied to bring about the end of the Scarlet

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:46.030
King’s terrible conquest.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:51.880
If there’s some unknown solution, waiting
out there in the dark, we may finally be able

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:56.860
to stop this rampaging Elder God from destroying
all we hold dear.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:12:00.480
But those are all very big Ifs...

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:06.640
Now go check out “SCP-001 - The Scarlet
King” and “Children of SCP-001 The Scarlet

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:12.600
King - Is SCP-999 Really His Son?” for more
on the endless disturbing mystery of the Scarlet

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:12.620
King.

